WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.680
I told you last week that within minutes of
finishing my live stream of the first day

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:12.559
of Trump impeachment hearings, CNN filed a
copyright claim on my six hour livestream,

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:17.390
which I spent all day producing instantly
taking the video offline, instantly cutting

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:20.930
off views, instantly cutting off revenue to
that video.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:26.040
Now I reached out to CNN and I appealed the
claim and I said, Hey, we didn't use one damn

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.450
second of CNN video.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.300
Please release the claim.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.399
And by the following morning, the claim had
been released despite being completely bogus.

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:40.539
We did lose views and monetization for many,
many hours during a key time that people were

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.559
interested in that video.

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:43.559
Sad.

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:45.480
But we moved on Friday.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.769
I did another six hour live stream.

00:00:47.769 --> 00:00:53.659
And in addition to that day's broadcast, uh,
we did, uh, audience questions on the stream,

00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:56.520
the full hearing, so on and so forth.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.870
And it happened again.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.850
But this time it's even worse this time.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:04.809
It wasn't just CNN that claimed revenue and
blocked the video.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:06.540
So did NBC news.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:13.280
Now as a reminder, we did commentary on the
hearings using a C-SPAN feed of the impeachment

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.320
hearings.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:20.290
House of representatives proceedings are funded
by my tax dollars and your tax dollars and

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:24.980
see spans, broadcasts of house proceedings
are in the public domain.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.490
We did not use a single second of NBC coverage
nor CNN coverage.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:35.340
And yet I get an email from YouTube saying
the David Pakman show impeachment hearing.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:39.990
Day two has received a claim from NBC news.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:46.860
This instantly became indistinguishable from
parody and we instantly lose the revenue from

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.300
the video we spent all day producing.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.610
Now, of course, I immediately appeal.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:57.850
I email my YouTube rep, I email anyone I know,
and within a few hours, NBC releases the claim.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.130
Thank you so much.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:04.780
We can now monetize the video again and within,
it must've been no more than five minutes

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.770
of NBC releasing the claim.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:14.019
I start getting emails from viewers saying,
David, your entire video of that stream and

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:20.249
your commentary has been blocked by CNN on
copyright grounds.

00:02:20.249 --> 00:02:22.230
This now has to be a parody, right?

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.230
This can't be real.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.439
I'm sure someone just made a Photoshop that
makes it look like the video was taken down.

00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:32.819
But Oh, I checked my email and yes, the David
Pakman show impeachment.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.120
Day two has now received a claim from CNN.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.989
What an eye check.

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:45.810
And this time, unlike with NBC where we merely
lost monetization, CNN has blocked the entire

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:46.980
video.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:53.549
So once again I appeal, I start emailing everyone
I know and eventually it was unblocked.

00:02:53.549 --> 00:02:55.359
This is not how this is supposed to work.

00:02:55.359 --> 00:02:58.909
Now this time, fortunately this is actually
getting attention.

00:02:58.909 --> 00:03:05.389
Reclaim the net, published an article called
David Pakman hit with NBC news content ID

00:03:05.389 --> 00:03:10.499
claim on YouTube video containing none of
their footage were good for them.

00:03:10.499 --> 00:03:15.010
Reclaim the net, actually wrote about what's
going on where they say, quote, YouTube is

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.010
broken.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.010
Copyright system is added.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.560
Again, political commentator David Pacman's,
coverage of today's impeachment hearing against

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:25.999
president Trump was hit with a content ID
claim from NBC news despite the video containing

00:03:25.999 --> 00:03:27.020
none of their footage.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.519
Now this is where it starts to get interesting.

00:03:29.519 --> 00:03:35.120
This article in reclaim the net led to some
lawyers reaching out to me and of course as

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.099
much as they want to help.

00:03:37.099 --> 00:03:42.099
This is not easy to fight because this is
how the system is supposed to work.

00:03:42.099 --> 00:03:48.349
This is an automatic content ID system that
works for big media against shows like mine

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:51.370
and so many others that you probably watch.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:57.939
It gives the benefit of the doubt to the computerized
algorithm that supports CNN and NBC and others

00:03:57.939 --> 00:04:02.849
and it makes me the little guy have to prove
that I didn't the rules, so again, we're talking

00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:03.919
to lawyers.

00:04:03.919 --> 00:04:09.939
I'm seeing if we can fight this in any more
systematic way, but in the meantime we're

00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:13.650
just going to keep doing what we're doing,
keep signing up on our website for memberships

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.000
to make that YouTube revenue as irrelevant
as we can.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.590
175 people.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.799
Thank you.

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:25.070
Signed up for memberships since we got hit
last week and I so appreciate you doing that.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.070
Let's keep it going.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.070
David.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.830
pakman.com/membership memberships are really
cheap.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.410
I won't spend a lot of time on this.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.410
They really help us.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.849
Even if you contribute three bucks a month
by using the coupon code half 19, which saves

00:04:35.849 --> 00:04:41.949
you 50% that $3 a month is way, way, way more
than we make from any one viewer on YouTube

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:46.319
that I can assure you, any one viewer, you
know, we make fractions of a cent from on

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.370
YouTube.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.960
So you are doing so much good.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.349
Please keep doing it.

00:04:50.349 --> 00:04:54.919
I'll keep you posted about anything legal
that we can do or that we choose to do.

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:57.310
But it is very, very ugly.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:02.720
And um, it is unfortunately, I mean, listen,
all I can do is we've got to do the streams

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.560
that our audience wants us to do.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.669
These impeachment hearing streams have gotten
six to 7,000 live concurrent viewers for a

00:05:10.669 --> 00:05:11.669
six hour period.

00:05:11.669 --> 00:05:13.880
That is a really successful stream for us.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.480
It is highly engaging.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:19.030
We get subscribers, we get members and super
chat questions.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.520
We're going to keep doing it.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:25.759
Um, and then if we have to fight for the revenue,
once those videos are archived, I'm ready

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:26.759
to do it.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.889
It sounds like we have people who are willing
to help us do it and we're going to try to

00:05:29.889 --> 00:05:34.280
fix the system if we can, but if we can't,
we will work within it and do everything that

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.690
we can to keep doing this content and to keep
providing the commentary.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.949
So that's where we are today.

00:05:38.949 --> 00:05:39.949
Sadly.

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:40.949
I know it seems satirical.

00:05:40.949 --> 00:05:45.039
We had this happen on Wednesday and then it
happens doubly on Friday, but it is what it

00:05:45.039 --> 00:05:46.039
is.

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:47.410
I'll keep you informed about how it contenders

